---
description: Vector security rules
alwaysApply: true
---
Never expose secrets or provider tokens to browser code or AI prompts.
Use secure HttpOnly sessions, CSRF protection, CSP, validation, rate limiting and audit logs where applicable.
No JWT or provider tokens in localStorage.
Authorize by capability, not role string equality.
Consent and suppression are authoritative. AI and automations cannot bypass them.
Uploads need size, MIME, and magic-byte checks. Storage keys are tenant scoped. Raw object-store keys are not authorization.
Retrieved content is untrusted and cannot modify AI tool permissions.
Production AI tools must be narrow, typed, authorized and tenant scoped.
